{
  "id": "s3",
  "title": "Scenario 3: Multi-Agent Research System",
  "subtitle": "CCAR-F Deep-Dive Study Guide",
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "definition",
      "term": [
        {
          "t": "text",
          "v": "Context"
        }
      ],
      "spans": [
        {
          "t": "text",
          "v": "A "
        },
        {
          "t": "strong",
          "v": "coordinator agent"
        },
        {
          "t": "text",
          "v": " (Claude Agent SDK) delegates to specialized subagents — web search, document analysis, synthesis, and report generation — to research topics and produce comprehensive, cited reports."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "definition",
      "term": [
        {
          "t": "text",
          "v": "Primary domains"
        }
      ],
      "spans": [
        {
          "t": "text",
          "v": "Agentic Architecture & Orchestration (D1) · Tool Design & MCP Integration (D2) · Context Management & Reliability (D5)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "divider"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "t": "text",
          "v": "Part 1: Hub-and-Spoke Orchestration (Task Statement 1.2)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "t": "text",
          "v": "Architecture rules"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "ordered": false,
      "items": [
        {
          "spans": [
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": "The "
            },
            {
              "t": "strong",
              "v": "coordinator"
            },
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": " owns: task decomposition, delegation, result aggregation, deciding "
            },
            {
              "t": "em",
              "v": "which"
            },
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": " subagents to invoke, error handling, and information routing."
            }
          ],
          "marker": "none",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "spans": [
            {
              "t": "strong",
              "v": "All inter-subagent communication routes through the coordinator"
            },
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": " (hub-and-spoke). Benefits: observability, consistent error handling, controlled information flow. Subagents never talk directly to each other."
            }
          ],
          "marker": "none",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "spans": [
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": "Subagents run with "
            },
            {
              "t": "strong",
              "v": "isolated context"
            },
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": " — they do NOT inherit the coordinator's conversation history automatically."
            }
          ],
          "marker": "none",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "t": "text",
          "v": "Dynamic invocation, not fixed pipelines"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "spans": [
        {
          "t": "text",
          "v": "A good coordinator analyzes the query and "
        },
        {
          "t": "strong",
          "v": "selects only the needed subagents"
        },
        {
          "t": "text",
          "v": " rather than always running the full pipeline. Simple factual query → maybe just web search + synthesis; deep comparison → all four."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "t": "text",
          "v": "The narrow-decomposition failure mode (sample Q7)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "spans": [
        {
          "t": "text",
          "v": "If the coordinator decomposes \"impact of AI on creative industries\" into only \"digital art / graphic design / photography,\" the report misses music, writing, and film — "
        },
        {
          "t": "strong",
          "v": "even though every subagent works perfectly"
        },
        {
          "t": "text",
          "v": ". Root cause: coordinator decomposition too narrow. Diagnostic habit: when coverage is incomplete but each agent succeeded, "
        },
        {
          "t": "strong",
          "v": "check what the coordinator assigned"
        },
        {
          "t": "text",
          "v": ", not the downstream agents."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "spans": [
        {
          "t": "text",
          "v": "Mitigations:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "ordered": false,
      "items": [
        {
          "spans": [
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": "Partition research scope to "
            },
            {
              "t": "strong",
              "v": "minimize duplication"
            },
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": " (distinct subtopics or source types per agent) "
            },
            {
              "t": "em",
              "v": "and"
            },
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": " maximize coverage."
            }
          ],
          "marker": "none",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "spans": [
            {
              "t": "strong",
              "v": "Iterative refinement loops"
            },
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": ": coordinator evaluates synthesis output for gaps → re-delegates targeted queries to search/analysis → re-invokes synthesis until coverage is sufficient."
            }
          ],
          "marker": "none",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "spans": [
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": "Coordinator prompts should specify "
            },
            {
              "t": "strong",
              "v": "research goals and quality criteria"
            },
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": ", not rigid step-by-step procedures — this preserves subagent adaptability."
            }
          ],
          "marker": "none",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "divider"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "t": "text",
          "v": "Part 2: Spawning Subagents and Passing Context (Task Statement 1.3)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "t": "text",
          "v": "Mechanics to memorize"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "ordered": false,
      "items": [
        {
          "spans": [
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": "Subagents are spawned via the "
            },
            {
              "t": "strong",
              "v": "Task tool"
            },
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": ". The coordinator's "
            },
            {
              "t": "code",
              "v": "allowedTools"
            },
            {
              "t": "strong",
              "v": " must include "
            },
            {
              "t": "code",
              "v": "\"Task\""
            },
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": " or it cannot spawn anything."
            }
          ],
          "marker": "none",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "spans": [
            {
              "t": "code",
              "v": "AgentDefinition"
            },
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": " configures each subagent type: description, system prompt, tool restrictions."
            }
          ],
          "marker": "none",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "spans": [
            {
              "t": "strong",
              "v": "Parallelism:"
            },
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": " emit "
            },
            {
              "t": "strong",
              "v": "multiple Task tool calls in a single coordinator response"
            },
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": " → subagents run in parallel. Emitting them across separate turns = sequential (slower)."
            }
          ],
          "marker": "none",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "spans": [
            {
              "t": "code",
              "v": "fork_session"
            },
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": ": create independent branches from a shared analysis baseline to explore divergent approaches."
            }
          ],
          "marker": "none",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "t": "text",
          "v": "Explicit context passing (the #1 gotcha)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "spans": [
        {
          "t": "text",
          "v": "Subagents share "
        },
        {
          "t": "strong",
          "v": "no memory"
        },
        {
          "t": "text",
          "v": " between invocations and inherit "
        },
        {
          "t": "strong",
          "v": "nothing"
        },
        {
          "t": "text",
          "v": ". Everything the synthesis agent needs — web search results, document analysis outputs — must be "
        },
        {
          "t": "strong",
          "v": "included directly in its prompt"
        },
        {
          "t": "text",
          "v": "."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "spans": [
        {
          "t": "text",
          "v": "Use "
        },
        {
          "t": "strong",
          "v": "structured formats separating content from metadata"
        },
        {
          "t": "text",
          "v": ":"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "json",
      "code": "{\n  \"claim\": \"EU AI Act enforcement began August 2026\",\n  \"evidence_excerpt\": \"...\",\n  \"source_url\": \"https://...\",\n  \"document_name\": \"EU Commission press release\",\n  \"publication_date\": \"2026-08-01\",\n  \"relevance_score\": 0.92\n}"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "spans": [
        {
          "t": "text",
          "v": "This preserves "
        },
        {
          "t": "strong",
          "v": "attribution"
        },
        {
          "t": "text",
          "v": " through handoffs and lets downstream agents reason about recency and reliability."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "divider"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "t": "text",
          "v": "Part 3: Tool Distribution Across Agents (Task Statement 2.3)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "t": "text",
          "v": "Principles"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "ordered": false,
      "items": [
        {
          "spans": [
            {
              "t": "strong",
              "v": "Too many tools degrades selection."
            },
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": " An agent with 18 tools instead of 4–5 makes unreliable choices — decision complexity scales with tool count."
            }
          ],
          "marker": "none",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "spans": [
            {
              "t": "strong",
              "v": "Agents misuse out-of-specialization tools"
            },
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": " (a synthesis agent with web search tools starts searching instead of synthesizing)."
            }
          ],
          "marker": "none",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "spans": [
            {
              "t": "strong",
              "v": "Scoped access:"
            },
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": " each agent gets only role-relevant tools, plus narrowly "
            },
            {
              "t": "strong",
              "v": "scoped cross-role tools for high-frequency needs"
            },
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": "."
            }
          ],
          "marker": "none",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "t": "text",
          "v": "The verify_fact pattern (sample Q9)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "spans": [
        {
          "t": "text",
          "v": "Synthesis frequently needs to verify claims; routing every verification through coordinator → web-search agent → back adds 2–3 round trips (+40% latency). If "
        },
        {
          "t": "strong",
          "v": "85% are simple fact-checks"
        },
        {
          "t": "text",
          "v": ", give the synthesis agent a "
        },
        {
          "t": "strong",
          "v": "scoped "
        },
        {
          "t": "code",
          "v": "verify_fact"
        },
        {
          "t": "strong",
          "v": " tool"
        },
        {
          "t": "text",
          "v": " for those, keeping coordinator-routed delegation for the complex 15%. This is "
        },
        {
          "t": "strong",
          "v": "least privilege"
        },
        {
          "t": "text",
          "v": ": enough capability for the common case, without over-provisioning (giving it "
        },
        {
          "t": "em",
          "v": "all"
        },
        {
          "t": "text",
          "v": " search tools) or speculative caching."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "t": "text",
          "v": "Constrained alternatives"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "spans": [
        {
          "t": "text",
          "v": "Replace generic tools with constrained ones: "
        },
        {
          "t": "code",
          "v": "fetch_url"
        },
        {
          "t": "text",
          "v": " → "
        },
        {
          "t": "code",
          "v": "load_document"
        },
        {
          "t": "text",
          "v": " that validates document URLs. Split overly generic tools: "
        },
        {
          "t": "code",
          "v": "analyze_document"
        },
        {
          "t": "text",
          "v": " → "
        },
        {
          "t": "code",
          "v": "extract_data_points"
        },
        {
          "t": "text",
          "v": ", "
        },
        {
          "t": "code",
          "v": "summarize_content"
        },
        {
          "t": "text",
          "v": ", "
        },
        {
          "t": "code",
          "v": "verify_claim_against_source"
        },
        {
          "t": "text",
          "v": ". Rename to eliminate overlap: "
        },
        {
          "t": "code",
          "v": "analyze_content"
        },
        {
          "t": "text",
          "v": " → "
        },
        {
          "t": "code",
          "v": "extract_web_results"
        },
        {
          "t": "text",
          "v": " with a web-specific description."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "t": "text",
          "v": "tool_choice options (also tested in Scenario 6)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "ordered": false,
      "items": [
        {
          "spans": [
            {
              "t": "code",
              "v": "\"auto\""
            },
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": " — model may answer in text OR call a tool"
            }
          ],
          "marker": "none",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "spans": [
            {
              "t": "code",
              "v": "\"any\""
            },
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": " — model MUST call some tool (its choice which)"
            }
          ],
          "marker": "none",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "spans": [
            {
              "t": "code",
              "v": "{\"type\": \"tool\", \"name\": \"...\"}"
            },
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": " — model MUST call that specific tool"
            }
          ],
          "marker": "none",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "divider"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "t": "text",
          "v": "Part 4: Error Propagation (Task Statements 2.2, 5.3)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "t": "text",
          "v": "The correct pattern (sample Q8)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "spans": [
        {
          "t": "text",
          "v": "When a subagent fails (e.g., web search timeout), return "
        },
        {
          "t": "strong",
          "v": "structured error context"
        },
        {
          "t": "text",
          "v": " to the coordinator:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "ordered": false,
      "items": [
        {
          "spans": [
            {
              "t": "strong",
              "v": "Failure type"
            },
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": " (timeout, access denied, ...)"
            }
          ],
          "marker": "none",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "spans": [
            {
              "t": "strong",
              "v": "What was attempted"
            },
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": " (the query)"
            }
          ],
          "marker": "none",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "spans": [
            {
              "t": "strong",
              "v": "Partial results"
            },
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": " gathered before failure"
            }
          ],
          "marker": "none",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "spans": [
            {
              "t": "strong",
              "v": "Potential alternative approaches"
            }
          ],
          "marker": "none",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "spans": [
        {
          "t": "text",
          "v": "This lets the coordinator decide intelligently: retry with a modified query, try an alternative source, or proceed with partials + annotate gaps."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "t": "text",
          "v": "Anti-patterns (all appear as distractors)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "ordered": false,
      "items": [
        {
          "spans": [
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": "Generic status after silent internal retries (\"search unavailable\") — hides context from the coordinator"
            }
          ],
          "marker": "dont",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "spans": [
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": "Returning empty results "
            },
            {
              "t": "strong",
              "v": "marked as successful"
            },
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": " — silently suppresses the error, corrupts the research"
            }
          ],
          "marker": "dont",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "spans": [
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": "Propagating the raw exception to a top-level handler that "
            },
            {
              "t": "strong",
              "v": "kills the whole workflow"
            },
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": " — one failure shouldn't end everything"
            }
          ],
          "marker": "dont",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "t": "text",
          "v": "Layered recovery"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "spans": [
        {
          "t": "text",
          "v": "Subagents handle "
        },
        {
          "t": "strong",
          "v": "local recovery for transient failures"
        },
        {
          "t": "text",
          "v": " themselves; they propagate only errors they "
        },
        {
          "t": "strong",
          "v": "cannot"
        },
        {
          "t": "text",
          "v": " resolve, together with partials and attempts. And always distinguish "
        },
        {
          "t": "strong",
          "v": "access failure"
        },
        {
          "t": "text",
          "v": " (couldn't search) from "
        },
        {
          "t": "strong",
          "v": "valid empty result"
        },
        {
          "t": "text",
          "v": " (searched fine, nothing matched)."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "t": "text",
          "v": "Coverage annotations"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "spans": [
        {
          "t": "text",
          "v": "Synthesis output should annotate which findings are "
        },
        {
          "t": "strong",
          "v": "well-supported"
        },
        {
          "t": "text",
          "v": " vs which topic areas have "
        },
        {
          "t": "strong",
          "v": "gaps due to unavailable sources"
        },
        {
          "t": "text",
          "v": " — the report is honest about its own blind spots."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "divider"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "t": "text",
          "v": "Part 5: Context, Provenance, and Conflicts (Task Statements 5.1, 5.6)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "t": "text",
          "v": "Position effects and budgets"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "ordered": false,
      "items": [
        {
          "spans": [
            {
              "t": "strong",
              "v": "Lost-in-the-middle:"
            },
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": " in long aggregated inputs, middle-section findings get dropped. Put a key-findings summary "
            },
            {
              "t": "strong",
              "v": "at the beginning"
            },
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": " and organize details under explicit section headers."
            }
          ],
          "marker": "none",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "spans": [
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": "When downstream agents have tight context budgets, modify "
            },
            {
              "t": "strong",
              "v": "upstream"
            },
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": " agents to return "
            },
            {
              "t": "strong",
              "v": "structured data"
            },
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": " (key facts, citations, relevance scores) instead of verbose prose and reasoning chains."
            }
          ],
          "marker": "none",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "spans": [
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": "Require subagents to include "
            },
            {
              "t": "strong",
              "v": "metadata"
            },
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": " (dates, source locations, methodological context) in structured outputs for accurate synthesis."
            }
          ],
          "marker": "none",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "t": "text",
          "v": "Provenance"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "ordered": false,
      "items": [
        {
          "spans": [
